# OWNER REVIEW
# The raffle at St. Prudence's (Key 3; levels/primrose/keys/raffle.gd). The first prize is one of Swyne's hypnotic toys.
# Buy a ticket, stuff the drum while the vicar's counting the float, and he draws. Nim wins; the vicar's never been so
# relieved. ("primrose/vicar_looking" is kept up to date by the script.)

~ start
[if primrose/raffle_won] => after
[if primrose/stuffed] => draw
[if primrose/ticket] => wait
Vicar: Raffle ticket? A pound a strip. All in aid of Decency.
Vicar: The first prize was donated by the Coalition. It's a, um. It's a toy. It hums.
- One strip, please. => buy
- Not tonight. => no

~ no
Vicar: No. No, quite right.

~ buy
Vicar: Lovely. Forty-seven. Lucky number. The draw's whenever I can face it.
set primrose/ticket

~ wait
Vicar: I'll draw when the drum's a bit fuller. Nobody's bought any. I can't think why.

~ draw
Vicar: Shall I? I shall. Here we go.
Vicar: And the winner is... number forty-seven! And forty-seven. And... they're all forty-seven.
Vicar [warm]: Oh, thank heavens. I mean, congratulations. Take it. Please. Take it a long way away.
[narrator] The first prize: a plush lamb with a spiral on its belly. It hums. Nim takes it a long way away.
set primrose/raffle_won

~ after
Vicar: The bake sale's raised eleven pounds. The raffle's raised my spirits.

~ drum
[if primrose/raffle_won] => after_drum
[if not primrose/ticket] => no_ticket
[if primrose/vicar_looking] => watched
[narrator] While the vicar counts the float, Nim writes forty-seven on every blank stub in reach and stuffs the drum.
set primrose/stuffed

~ no_ticket
[narrator] A drum of raffle tickets. None of them is hers. Yet.

~ watched
Vicar: Ahem. Did you want something, dear?

~ after_drum
[narrator] The drum's empty. It was only ever forty-sevens.
